# The base: what a POS system is without init and kernel, as in a
# container. The shell, the core utilities, the login and account tools,
# and transfer with curl. Not a minimal set: a generally functional
# userland (BUILD.md "Base stage"). A pos reference holds it with
# core-libs, so pos-sdk and pos-extras builds can take its tools and
# libraries.
# POS's own integration: os-release, the PAM stack, /etc/profile and
# pos-preferences (an output of pos-integration).
pos-integration-base
# libsystemd and libudev (an output of systemd): util-linux, procps and
# shadow link them; systemd itself is the system stage's.
systemd-libs
util-linux
bash
coreutils
findutils
grep
sed
gawk
tar
gzip
cpio
less
gettext
shadow
sudo
# User utilities: libmagic file type detection, command lookup.
file
which
# Process tools: ps, top, free, pgrep, sysctl, watch, w, uptime.
procps
# Transfer: curl and libcurl (HTTP/2 with nghttp2). pos-kernel downloads
# with it; git in pos-extras links libcurl.
nghttp2
curl
